=== 2026-09-30 16:20 PDT - KDE screen-lock "emergency" blackout: root cause found and fixed ===

  CONTEXT (host desktop, not Podman/Quadlet)
   Symptom: after suspend/resume, black screen with white text: "THE SCREEN LOCKER
   IS BROKEN AND UNLOCKING IS NOT POSSIBLE ANYMORE ... loginctl unlock-session7".
   User first read it as a hijack/forced lockout.

  DIAGNOSIS (read-only inspection)
   - Message is KWin's OWN emergency screen (org_kde_ksld_emergency in
     libkwin.so.6.6.6; text shipped in kscreenlocker.mo, 42 locales,
     PO-Revision-Date 2023-03-10). Zero third-party hits -> NOT a compromise.
     Upstream typo: "unlock-session7" missing the space; correct cmd is
     "loginctl unlock-session 7".
   - KDE's own instructions failed here for two reasons: getty@tty1 is
     inactive (dead) so Ctrl+Alt+F1 shows a black screen, and the numbered
     command has no space. tty3/tty6 have live gettys.
   - Trigger: kscreenlocker_greet SIGSEGV x4 at 15:13:50-51
     (pids 3767739/3767763/3767784/3767808), then KWin logged
     "Everything else failed. Need to put Greeter in emergency mode."

  ROOT CAUSE (PROVEN - three-state isolated test)
   A CORRUPTED user fontconfig cache at ~/.cache/fontconfig.
   - GDB: SIGSEGV at libfontconfig.so.1 +0xc4fc -> FcCharSetHasChar() ->
     QFontEngineMultiFontConfig::shouldLoadFontEngineForCharacter() ->
     QTextEngine::shapeText() -> QQmlObjectCreator::finalize (greeter QML).
   - Same +0xc4fc/FcCharSetHasChar frame appears in plasmashell and
     kioworker (SVG thumbnail) coredumps -> ONE bug, many Qt/QML victims.
   - Three-state proof: good cache rc=0 | restore corrupt cache rc=139 |
     good cache rc=0; isolated clean $HOME rc=0.
   - fc-cache had reported 10 "invalid cache file: <hash>-le64.cache-9";
     Qt read cache-9 directly and faulted while fc-cache merely skipped it.

  TIMELINE
   greeter worked 07:20 and 10:46 -> user font cache rebuilt 14:23:48-49 ->
   greeter crashed from 15:13 onward. No package upgrade (unattended-upgrades
   06:55 touched only openssl/libheif), no OOM (0), no hardware error on nvme0n1.
   fontconfig lib unchanged since 2026-01-21.

  FIX APPLIED (16:15 PDT) - non-destructive
   1. mv ~/.cache/fontconfig /tmp/fontconfig-cache-bak-1790810150 (preserved)
   2. fc-cache -f -v   -> succeeded, no invalid-cache lines on re-run
   3. kscreenlocker_greet --testing -> rc=0, "Locked ... Unlocked"
   4. re-tested x2 for determinism: rc=0, rc=0
   Session 7 never killed: Active=yes State=active LockedHint=no; kwin 4421 /
   plasmashell 4556 / all 15 containers untouched.

  RECOVERY USED BY OPERATOR
   loginctl unlock-session 7 (from tty3; space required). Session unlocked
   without terminating anything.

  FINDINGS FILE
   /home/scottw/Desktop/ONGOING PROBLEM.txt (sections 1-10 diagnosis,
   section 11 resolution/prevention).

  RESIDUAL / FOLLOW-UP (separate from lock bug)
   - kwalletd6: 26,969 SIGABRT Sep 27-29 as uid 993 (alwayson-sales), Qt
     event-dispatcher fatal, unrelated to fontconfig; last crash Sep 29 14:20,
     not running now. Investigate separately.
   - getty@tty1 dead -> KDE lock instructions unusable. Enable if desired:
     systemctl enable getty@tty1
   - /dev/sdc1 Buffer I/O errors; NVMe error count 1315->1319. Watch, run
     SMART at leisure. Did NOT cause this incident.
   - sddm autologin has empty User= (20-kubuntu.conf). Left as-is (no change).

