2026-09-30 — OUTBOUND federation fixed and proven (reverse follow achieved)
  SYMPTOM: every signed outbound fetch returned HTTP 401. Search/resolve returned
    0 accounts, so no follow or post could ever reach a remote server, even
    though raw HTTPS from the container worked (WebFinger 200, actor fetch 200).

  ROOT CAUSE: Account.representative (the instance actor, id -99) had
    username "300x3.com" and, critically, EMPTY uri, inbox_url and
    shared_inbox_url. Mastodon signs every outgoing request on behalf of that
    actor; a signature from an actor with no inbox/id is rejected by remotes
    with 401. The row was created at the boot that ran under the wrong
    LOCAL_DOMAIN, and only before_create callbacks populate those columns, so a
    domain correction never repaired it.

  FIX: set username=mastodon.internal, domain=nil, and the three URIs from the
    current LOCAL_DOMAIN:
      uri               https://mastodon.300x3.com/users/mastodon.internal
      inbox_url         https://mastodon.300x3.com/users/mastodon.internal/inbox
      shared_inbox_url  https://mastodon.300x3.com/inbox
    After this, FetchResourceService returns HTTP 200 for a remote actor.

  PROOF (both directions now):
    outbound  @bot follows @Gargron@mastodon.social - remote actor resolved and
              follow created, Follow uri https://mastodon.300x3.com/f7ccfd56-...
    inbound   mastodon.social delivered a signed activity to POST /inbox (202)
              and the resulting relationship is recorded as
              "@Gargron@mastodon.social -> @bot", i.e. a REVERSE FOLLOW.
    1 remote account now persisted (was 0).
