2026-09-30 — offline machine is a normal state, not a failure (operator)
  Operator: fabrication machines are powered on only while in use and are off
  otherwise; they are not expected to be continuously reachable.

  The collector previously counted an unreachable machine as a failure and
  exited 1, so the timer logged an error on every pass while the machine was
  simply switched off. It now distinguishes the two:
    - unreachable (ECONNREFUSED/EHOSTUNREACH/ENETUNREACH/ETIMEDOUT/timeout) ->
      counted as "offline", logged as skipped, NOT a failure
    - reachable but returning unusable data, or an HTTP error response ->
      still a genuine failure
  HTTPError is checked before URLError because it subclasses it; a machine that
  answers with 401/500 has responded and must not be classed as offline.
  Verified: offline machine -> "0 ok, 0 failed, 1 offline", unit Result=success,
  exit 0. Against a local Moonraker-shaped mock -> "1 ok" with a full record,
  proving collection still works when a machine is up. a_fab still holds the
  earlier verified printer-01 rows.

  Domoticz (:6144, :8080) left bound and untouched: not connected to anything
  and intentionally so for the foreseeable future (operator decision
  2026-09-30). Recorded in the README as a known non-ao-* listener so the "no
  public listener" claim is read accurately rather than overstated.

