  Before installing, established what "Corda 5.2.2" actually refers to. The
  install cannot be performed from this host without operator-supplied R3
  credentials, so nothing was downloaded and nothing was changed.

  EVIDENCE
    - General egress is fine: repo1.maven.org 200, github.com 200.
      software.r3.com returns 403 for anonymous requests, with and without a
      browser User-Agent, at the root and at the known Corda 4.14.2 artifact
      path. So the 403 is the host refusing unauthenticated access, not a
      network fault on this machine.
    - Corda 5 is the R3 COMMERCIAL platform. The open-source Corda repository
      (github.com/corda/corda) has no 5.x release at all; its newest release is
      Corda 4.1 (2019). There is no public 5.2.2 artefact on Maven Central
      (com/r3/corda returns nothing) and none in apt.
    - No local copy, cache, archive or container image of Corda 5 exists on this
      host. The only Corda artefacts present are backup/restore scripts, the
      sale-receipt forms, the runbook, and the 2026-09-28 V4 retirement log,
      whose download log records Corda 4.14.2 from the R3 artifactory.

  WHY NOT PROCEED
    - Obtaining Corda 5.2.2 requires R3 account credentials and a licence. I
      will not work around a vendor access control, and will not pull jars from
      an unofficial mirror.
    - Corda 4.14.2 is NOT an acceptable substitute: the operator retired it
      deliberately on 2026-09-28 ("delete corda 4 and its h2 databases and we
      will work with corda 5"). Reinstalling it would reverse that decision.

  TO UNBLOCK, the operator must supply one of:
    1. R3 credentials plus the intended Corda 5.2.2 distribution, or
    2. the exact download URL/location for the Corda 5.2.2 artefacts, or
    3. confirmation to switch to the newest open-source Corda (4.14.x) instead,
       which is a different platform from the Corda 5 the design assumes.

  Note this is independent of the pending key and certificate ceremony: even with
  the software in place, ST-09 stays Blocked until that operator step is done.

