2026-09-30 — QGC-over-LoRa investigation closed as an outstanding item
  Asked to set up QGroundControl with a LoRa drone link encrypted with RNS.
  Investigated rather than built, because the design has a hard constraint.

  WHAT IS ALREADY CORRECT AND NEEDS NO WORK
    The desktop DRONE-RADIO is a configured Reticulum RNodeInterface on
    /dev/ttyUSB0 (via by-path pci-0000:05:00.0-usb-0:1:1.0-port0),
    917 MHz / 250 kHz / SF7 / CR5 / 17 dBm, discoverable = no. That matches
    README 9.2.2 exactly, and RNS encryption is inherent to RNode. So the air
    link between the desktop and the RPi5 Waveshare radio is already set up.
    PEOPLE-RADIO (ttyUSB1, 915 MHz / 125 kHz) is likewise configured.
    Correction to an earlier statement of mine: I first claimed MeshChatX was
    "all TCP, no LoRa". That was wrong - my parser failed on the [[double
    bracket]] syntax. The real count is 32 interfaces: 29 TCPClientInterface,
    1 BackboneInterface and 2 RNodeInterface.

  THREE CONSTRAINTS THAT SHAPE THE SOLUTION
    1. QGroundControl v5.1.0 (AppImage) cannot speak RNS. It is MAVLink-only,
       with UDP/TCP/serial/SiK links. No Reticulum driver or plugin exists.
    2. Reticulum ships no MAVLink transport, so something must translate. That
       is code to be written, not a configuration change.
    3. The desktop Reticulum stack runs INSIDE ReticulumMeshChatX (pid 4961),
       which holds /dev/ttyUSB0 open on fd 53u. A second RNS instance would
       contend for the same port, because Reticulum has no way to attach to
       another process's embedded stack.

  DECISION (operator): the RPi5 Waveshare end terminates the link and runs the
  bridge. That avoids all three constraints, leaves MeshChatX and the working
  chat path untouched, and matches 9.2.2, which already describes a QGC session
  on the RPi5 for out-of-range operation.

  DEFERRED, not started. Recorded as work-queue item 37 in section 19.4 with the
  three constraints, so the investigation is not repeated. Blocked on the RPi5
  address and SSH access: it is absent from the dnsmasq lease file, the ARP
  cache, and every config in the repository. A ping sweep of 10.42.0.0/24 found
  only the desktop itself (10.42.0.1), the 3D printer being powered off.

  No configuration was changed. A standalone Reticulum venv was started during
  the investigation and removed at the operator's direction; scratch files and
  the scan were cleaned up.

