2026-09-30 — Desktop "windows closing themselves" (Dolphin et al.) DIAGNOSED
and REPAIRED. The apps were not being closed by anything; they were
SIGSEGV-crashing the moment they opened a window, which is what the operator
saw as a window appearing and vanishing, with Dr Konqi reporting each crash.
coredumpctl showed libfontconfig.so.1 at the top of every affected backtrace
(dolphin, kioworker, kscreenlocker_greet). Root cause was a corrupted
fontconfig cache in /home/scottw/.cache/fontconfig/: cache files written in an
incompatible on-disk format (cache-10 / cache-12 alongside the host's cache-9
set) and then partially written, which made libfontconfig return garbage font
records — KaTeX woff files advertised with empty charsets — and segfault during
the font lookup every Qt app performs at startup. Repair, in order: full backup
of all cache files to /tmp/fontconfig-bak-1790827342 (nothing deleted before
backup); foreign-version caches moved aside to that backup rather than deleted;
forced rebuild with "fc-cache -f -v" giving 0 invalid entries; verified
fc-match "Noto Sans" -> NotoSans-Regular.ttf, sans-serif and monospace
resolving correctly and Helvetica -> NimbusSans; smoke-tested dolphin, which
stayed open. No new coredumpctl entries after 20:28 PDT, before the repair.
Prevention added as systemd --user units only, no root and no new listening
port: ao-font-cache-gate.sh/.service with a 5-minute ao-font-cache-gate.timer,
which rebuilds, validates and quarantines foreign-version or invalid cache
files (v2 verified clean: "fc-cache rc=0; quarantined=0; expect-v=9", no false
positives), and ao-fontconfig-watch.sh/.service, a 3-second poller on the cache
directory that logs the writer to ~/Desktop/SYSTEM LOCKOUT/WATCH-LOG.txt so a
reappearance can be attributed. The identity of the process that originally
wrote the corrupt caches is NOT confirmed — candidates (snap/flatpak/container
fc-cache builds) were narrowed but none proven, as the journal had no entry at
the relevant times; the guards make any such writer harmless rather than
removing it. Findings written to
/home/scottw/Desktop/SYSTEM LOCKOUT/FIX-RESULTS.txt.

