2026-10-01  ao-build-update: promotion path + update runbook
================================================================================

SCOPE
  Completed the update process inside the ao-build-update network. Acquisition
  existed and was verified; promotion had no tool and no written procedure, so
  the path stopped at "here is a digest". Added both.

FILES ADDED
  scripts/build-update/promote-image-digest.sh   promotion helper
  docs/runbooks/software-update.md               the operator procedure
  README.md                                      cross-reference only

WHAT THE HELPER DOES
  Edits exactly one Image= line in exactly one .container under
  quadlet/<domain>/, then prints what to run next. It does not deploy and does
  not restart: reviewing a diff and applying it stay two separate decisions.
  It refuses, with exit 3 and no change, when the reference is unqualified,
  carries no sha256 digest, has a malformed digest, the unit has zero or
  multiple Image= lines, or the change would swap registry host. A
  cross-registry move is a deliberate act, not a version bump.
  --check reports the current reference and whether it is pinned.

VERIFICATION
  bash -n clean. Tested against a scratch copy of the operations tree, never a
  live unit; quadlet/operations/ao-grafana.container confirmed byte-identical
  before and after.
    --check on a pinned unit            -> 0, DIGEST-PINNED
    --check on the unpinned GUI unit    -> 0, NOT PINNED (correctly flagged)
    missing arguments                   -> 2
    non-container argument              -> 2
    floating tag as new reference       -> 3
    unqualified reference               -> 3
    malformed digest                    -> 3
    cross-registry swap                 -> 3
    real promotion                      -> 0, exactly one line changed
    re-run with same digest             -> 0, no-op
  Promotion recorded in logs/audit.log with old and new digest.
  Every command in the runbook was executed as written: the inventory loop, the
  --check invocation, validate-quadlet-domain.sh on the operations domain (exit
  0, "4 unit(s) deployed, no drift"), and the existence of all three validation
  scripts. The inventory loop independently re-confirmed the only two unpinned
  images: ao-sim-fabrication-gui-gz (local build, ao-sim-fabrication) and
  ao-ardupilot-sitl (:latest, not deployed).
  Acquisition regression unchanged: pinned -> 0, unpinned -> 4, unqualified -> 2.
  Network isolation check green; adapter unit starts clean (exit 0).

OWNERSHIP, PER OPERATOR
  GAZEBO files are owned by ao-sim-fabrication. Recorded in README 5.2.1 as a
  scope boundary: builds belong to the domain that consumes the image, and
  ao-build-update does not acquire, rebuild, or promote them.

OPEN, FOR THE OPERATOR
  - Enabling the ao-build-update unit permanently.
  - Whether the component should be renamed ao-update, now that image builds
    are confirmed to belong to ao-sim-fabrication. README 5.2.1 records the
    boundary; the naming decision is still open.

