================================================================================
2026-10-01  RNS public/private split: representation settled, handed off
================================================================================

OPERATOR CLARIFICATION, which corrected my own wrong assumption:
  "NO, THEY AREN'T. QGROUNDCONTROL WILL EVENTUALLY BE SETUP TO USE RNS TO
   COMMUNICATE TO IT VIA ENCRYPTION."
I had assumed QGC would sit outside RNS on the raw LoRa link. That was wrong.
Because drone traffic is intended to travel THROUGH the one stack, a single
stack is the correct design rather than a compromise, and two installations
would break it because Routing IDs are meaningful only within one stack.

WHAT THE SEPARATION ACTUALLY IS
  Not two installations, and not routing-id ranges. This RNS has no
  interface_routing_id at all - confirmed from the bytecode. It separates by
  INTERFACE MODE, and it is ALREADY configured correctly:
    [[PEOPLE-RADIO]]  915 MHz / 125 kHz   selected_interface_mode = 1  (FULL)
    [[DRONE-RADIO]]   917 MHz / 250 kHz   selected_interface_mode = 7  (INTERNAL)
                                          + mode = internal, discoverable = no
  rnstatus confirms at runtime: PEOPLE-RADIO Up/Mode Full, DRONE-RADIO
  Up/Mode Internal, both with live signal figures. 43 interfaces up in total.

  So the drone path is private by RNS's own mechanism, and the public LoRaWAN
  path is separate. Nothing needs to change to achieve the separation.

PODMAN SHAPE, VERIFIED BUT NOT BUILT
  Device pass-through works: podman run -v /dev/ao-drone-radio:... and the same
  for people-radio both present and read the device. A container would need two
  networks - ao-field for the field/drone side plus a new non-internal egress
  network, the same ao-reporting-egress pattern ao-grafana and ao-metabase
  already use - with the web UI on 127.0.0.1:18000.
  NOT BUILT. It changes network topology, isolation policy and adds serial
  passthrough to a container, so it needs operator approval. It is also not
  needed to fix the security question, because mode already enforces the split.

  Open: inside a container the device appears as nobody:nobody although the host
  side is 0660 root:dialout, so a GroupAdd=dialout plus a matching service user
  would be needed. Recorded, not solved.

TOPOLOGY GRAPHIC: NOT MINE, HANDED OFF
  Wrote "COORDINATION BETWEEN AI/J. 2026-10-01-rns-topology-representation.md"
  for whichever session takes the graphic. It carries the measured facts, what
  NOT to draw (two stacks; routing-id ranges), the Podman shape, and three open
  findings. The graphic is generated from config/platform/topology-model.yaml by
  scripts/operations/generate-topology.py; I touched neither.

  Flagged for whoever draws it: the operator brief in "X - README - GITHUB
  REVIEW-20261001.txt" spells the drone radio "DONE-RADIO". The RNS config, the
  udev symlink and all live evidence say DRONE-RADIO. Believed to be a typo, but
  worth confirming rather than drawing.

